    runtime: a membership taken back ends the callers of the member's instance that has no code
    
    The removal walk (compiler §5.5) ended the code of each instance of a method at the set compiled at the member,
    with its callers, through the instance's CodeInstances. Code that names the instance alone, with no code of
    its own (an `applicable` or `hasmethod` folded through the membership), kept its answer after the membership
    was taken back. The walk now ends the instance's backedges too, as a method's deletion does
    (`invalidate_backedges`).
    
    Reference: compiler §5.5 (taken back: the instances at the member end, with their callers), §5.6.
    Test: experiments/implementation/audit/set_folds.jl (E-542); experiments/implementation/w171/gates.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

